{
  "module": "MReactorWake.tla",
  "status": "refinement",
  "summary": "How a thread gets a reactor thread to run a task (net/reactor.rs): Link::notify marks `dirty` once and pushes a Run message, Shared::send records a wake-up debt and pays it unless a hold is active, Shared::release clears the hold and then pays, and the reactor sets `sleeping`, re-checks its queue, then polls; every published frame is taken without readiness, tick or timeout once the holds are released. In the default single-owner runtime the core thread alone sends and holds, and releases at the end of each pass. With --delivery-shards K >= 1 the shard workers hold as well and, since the validation of the lot 10 head, release before they wait. At 9dfd568 a shard kept its hold through its wait: no invariant was broken, but the release the liveness property assumes came as late as the timeout of that wait (hold-kept-liveness, kept as the counterexample of that behaviour).",
  "issues": [
    648
  ],
  "tests": [
    "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net/reactor.rs",
    "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/runtime_tests/sharded_faults.rs"
  ],
  "replays": [
    {
      "file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net/reactor.rs",
      "test": "a_notification_runs_the_task_once_and_a_waiting_task_is_ticked"
    },
    {
      "file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net/reactor.rs",
      "test": "a_held_wake_up_is_given_when_the_hold_ends"
    },
    {
      "file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net/reactor.rs",
      "test": "a_task_runs_on_readiness_and_rests_between_events"
    },
    {
      "file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/runtime_tests/sharded_faults.rs",
      "test": "an_idle_shard_waits_without_holding_the_reactors_wake_ups"
    }
  ],
  "not_replayed": "The lost-message counterexamples (mut-*) need a chosen schedule of two or three threads; no deterministic test replays them. The two debt mutants need a second sending thread beside the one that holds, which the default runtime does not have. The premise of hold-kept-liveness, a holder that waits with its hold, is replayed by an_idle_shard_waits_without_holding_the_reactors_wake_ups, which fails on 9dfd568; the delay it caused is not measured. The cited tests show a notification running an idle task once, a held wake-up given at the release, and an idle task resting, on real threads.",
